<p>I think a bigger potential problem with chucking it into space would be…what if it loses its momentum due to a collission, or brushing too close to a planetoid, and falls into the gravity well of another planet or even the sun? We'd stand a good chance of suddenly losing a rather sizable amount of mass from the solar system, which could wreak havoc on the orbital dynamics..assuming it doesn't fall into the sun and swallow a sizable portion of *its* mass, leading to a potential acellerated nova or supernova event.</p>
